# Before any changes are made to this file, please check with the Distribution
# team so that the changes can be coordinated between the cookbooks and the packages.
Protocol 2
StrictModes yes
MaxStartups 10:30:60
Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com,aes128-gcm@openssh.com,aes256-ctr,aes192-ctr,aes128-ctr
# Re-enable the legacy ssh-rsa (RSA + SHA-1) public-key signature algorithm.
# OpenSSH >= 8.8 (Ubuntu 24.04/Noble ships 9.6) drops ssh-rsa from the default
# accepted set, keeping only rsa-sha2-256/512. AWSM provisions instances over
# SSH using net-ssh 2.9.2 (ey_slater), which predates RSA-SHA2 and can only
# sign RSA keys with ssh-rsa; without this, every AWSM provisioning/config
# login is rejected ("SSH access unsuccessful") and Chef never runs. Append
# (do not replace) so the modern rsa-sha2-* algorithms remain enabled.
PubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms +ssh-rsa
HostKeyAlgorithms +ssh-rsa
PasswordAuthentication no
ChallengeResponseAuthentication no
Subsystem sftp /usr/lib/openssh/sftp-server
UseDNS no
UsePAM yes
PrintMotd no
PrintLastLog no
LogLevel VERBOSE
AcceptEnv EY_USER
